cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DeepSpace Plant-Stress to Germinating-Seed Decoder (DSRS + GSAD) and seed-susceptibility atlas"
message: "If you use this software, data, or atlas, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Barker
    given-names: Richard
    affiliation: "Purdue University; The Collaborative Science Environment, PBC"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # placeholder — replace with real ORCID
abstract: >-
  Two FAIR tools for plant space biology: DSRS (DeepSpace Stress-Recognition System) recognizes which
  space stressor a transcriptomic signature resembles, and GSAD (Germinating-Seed AutoDecoder) models a
  bulk transcriptome's predicted effect on dry/germinating-seed cell types. Includes the DeepSpace
  seed-susceptibility atlas across microgravity, low-oxygen, radiation, tropism, and magnetic-field stressors.
keywords:
  - plant space biology
  - microgravity
  - germination
  - single-cell atlas
  - Arabidopsis thaliana
  - npj Microgravity
license: MIT
